 The [dated harness review](reviews/2026-09-06-harness-review.md) preserves the earlier review baseline.
 Registered-project/native inventory, saved views and a shared intervention inbox are now integrated.
 Revision-bound verification and full multi-worktree scheduling remain separate architectural work.
+
+## Incident-driven operator recovery and event delivery
+
+The operator CLI is self-describing. Use `fleet --help` or `fleet <command> --help`; do not inspect a
+versioned plugin cache directory to discover syntax. Invoke only the current plugin root:
+
+```sh
+node "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/fleet.mjs" --help
+```
+
+### Wait without shell polling
+
+`result --wait` defaults to 10 minutes and uses the supervisor's state-change signal. A timeout returns
+the still-current lane and `timedOut:true`; it does not convert a running/queued lane into failure.
+For broader background observation, `watch` waits on one existing supervisor for a meaningful
+terminal/controller/intervention/queue-stall/continuation-unknown transition. It does not create a
+supervisor or model turn.
+
+Fleet also installs an `asyncRewake` Stop hook. When Claude becomes idle while Fleet has live work, one
+bounded watcher is registered for that Claude session/workspace. A meaningful transition exits with
+feedback that wakes Claude to inspect exact Fleet evidence and continue the original user request.
+Duplicate watchers are suppressed; timeout/no-supervisor exits silently. This replaces `until ... sleep`
+loops without creating a reasoning-agent polling loop.
+
+### Recover ambiguous continuation reservations
+
+Probe first:
+
+```sh
+node "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/fleet.mjs" reconcile --workspace . --lane <id> --json
+```
+
+Fleet releases a writer reservation automatically only when runtime history proves the follow-up did not
+start. If runtime history proves a turn did start, Fleet preserves/rebinds that truth. If evidence remains
+ambiguous, manual `--assume-not-started` requires an explicit evidence reference plus `--confirm`; do not
+edit `state.json` out of band.
+
+An `outcome_unknown`/`interrupted` lane can be resolved only with evidence:
+
+```sh
+node "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/fleet.mjs" resolve --workspace . --lane <id> \
+  --evidence-ref <ref> --outcome complete --confirm --json
+```
+
+After terminal truth is settled, `archive --lane <id>` hides the lane from default status without deleting
+its evidence/history. `status --archived` includes archived lanes.
+
+### Cancellation without losing touched-file truth
+
+`cancel <laneId> --workspace .` is the short preview. It returns the exact thread/turn identity plus bounded
+`touchedFiles`. A human typing the CLI may add `--confirm`; Fleet internally performs a fresh identity-bound
+preview before the cancellation request. Claude-controlled cancellation still shows the preview to the
+user and confirms the exact structured token/identity. Cancellation never reverts touched files.
+
+### Worktree ledgers and model catalog freshness
+
+Without `--workspace`, Fleet resolves cwd to its actual Git worktree root. An explicitly supplied workspace
+is never silently rewritten. If that ledger is empty while registered sibling worktrees in the same Git
+repository have lanes, status emits a bounded `workspaceWarning`; it never merges their control authority.
+Cross-worktree retry lineage uses `<workspaceKey>:<laneId>` and is validated against the registered source
+ledger before admission.
+
+`models` reports `discoveredAt`/`ageMs`. If the root Codex config names a model absent from the connected
+catalog, Fleet reports the mismatch. `models --refresh` may restart only an idle Fleet-owned app-server; it
+never guesses an alias or changes the user's configured model.
+
+### Verification and false-green prevention
+
+Generated contracts separate `verificationPlan.start`, `.completion`, and `.controller`. A completion-only
+build/database/browser limitation must not become a reason to spend a full turn and write nothing. Checks
+are recorded as `passed`, `failed`, `skipped`, or `blocked`. Read-only pytest can use
+`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` and `-p no:cacheprovider` when cache writes are incidental. Mutation checks must
+assert the intended mutation actually applied before interpreting a green result; Windows tasks must not
+assume `/tmp` is visible to native tooling. Visual/CSS/layout claims require browser/image evidence or stay
+explicitly unverified.
+
+### Cancellation is an interrupt protocol, not an undo
+
+The short human CLI form still performs the same identity-bound preview internally. `accepted: true` means Codex accepted the interrupt request; Fleet does not release writer capacity or claim the lane is stopped until `terminalObserved: true` arrives. If acknowledgement is delayed, status remains live/cancelling and the completion watcher will surface the eventual terminal transition. `touchedFiles` is evidence only; cancellation never rolls those files back.
