index 7dc7900..e4f4b5e 100644
--- a/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md
+++ b/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md
@@ -146,3 +146,37 @@ node scripts/check-doc-links.mjs
 Platform-specific failures should include the runner/OS, Node version, Claude version, Codex
 version and the exact failing command. See [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md) for the expected
 report shape.
+
+## A lane is queued but nothing is actually running
+
+Read `status --summary --json` and inspect `queueBlocker`. Fleet distinguishes capacity, active-writer,
+unresolved-continuation reservation, and scheduler ordering. `queued` is not proof of progress. If an
+unknown follow-up reservation holds the writer lock, run `reconcile --lane <id>`; never delete the field
+from state storage manually.
+
+## `status` says no lanes but I know a worktree has them
+
+Fleet state is keyed to the physical worktree. Omitting `--workspace` resolves cwd to the current Git
+worktree root. If an explicitly selected/root ledger is empty while sibling registered worktrees have lanes,
+status returns `workspaceWarning` with bounded related-ledger counts. Use the exact worktree or `fleet projects`;
+Fleet deliberately does not merge writer/control authority across worktrees.
+
+## I upgraded Codex but a new model is missing
+
+Run `models --json` and inspect `discoveredAt`, `ageMs`, and `configuredModelPresent`. If the user's root
+Codex config names a model missing from the current app-server catalog, run `models --refresh` only when
+Fleet is idle. If still absent, verify the installed Codex version/account capability. Do not hard-code a
+model alias or fall back silently.
+
+## A completion gate is impossible inside the lane sandbox
+
+Do not make it a start gate. Generated templates separate start, completion, and controller checks. A real
+DB, browser rendering, full build subprocess, network font download, or read-only-incompatible cache write
+can be `blocked`/`skipped` and delegated to the controller. This is different from a failed implementation.
+For read-only pytest, prefer `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` plus `-p no:cacheprovider` where applicable.
+
+## I cancelled a lane but files changed
+
+This is expected: cancellation stops owned execution; it is not rollback. The preview and accepted cancel
+response include bounded `touchedFiles`. Inspect/preserve/revert those changes with normal Git/project tools
+before assuming the worktree is clean.
