new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ad31ee7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/reviews/2026-09-09-incident-findings-closure.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# Sep 7–8 Fleet incident findings — closure matrix
+
+This file maps the measured operator incidents to the source changes in the stacked hardening series.
+It distinguishes a Fleet fix from an external project prerequisite. “Guarded” means Fleet cannot create
+the missing external capability, but it now fails early or records `skipped` / `blocked` / `unverified`
+instead of turning missing evidence into a green result.
+
+| Finding | Disposition | Closure |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 1.1 / 3.1 invalid final JSON after useful mutable work | Fixed in #14 | One same-thread report-only repair, read-only/network-off; a second malformed report remains reconciliation-required. |
+| 1.2 / 2.1 sandbox gate failures (`spawn EPERM`, Python environment) | Fixed/guarded | Zero-inference nested-process and Python provenance preflight in #14; #15 templates route unavailable full-build/DB/browser checks to explicit controller/skipped/blocked states. |
+| 1.3 / 3.10 oversized multi-surface lanes | Fixed as orchestration policy | Shared stable context is separated from task text; default topology is <=2 coherent surfaces / <=1 migration per lane. Fleet does not use brittle semantic auto-splitting heuristics. |
+| 1.4 / 2.8 cancel and terminal-history ergonomics | Fixed in #15 | `cancel <laneId>`, `archive`, `resolve`, `reconcile`, help/examples, identity-bound confirmation and retained history. |
+| 1.5 misplaced `modelPolicy` / stale model catalog | Fixed across #14/#15 | Root-placement diagnostic; catalog timestamp/age; idle `models --refresh`; config/catalog mismatch hint without alias substitution. |
+| 1.6 / 3.5 wrong worktree ledger | Fixed in #15 | Implicit cwd resolves to its Git worktree root. Explicit workspace stays exact and an empty ledger warns about sibling worktree ledgers instead of silently saying “nothing exists.” |
+| 1.7 / 2.2 completion gate mistaken for start gate | Fixed across #14/#15 | Structured `verificationPlan.start/completion/controller`; templates explicitly prohibit treating completion gates as permission to avoid implementation. |
+| 1.8 / 1.11 missing completion notification | Fixed in #15 | One local event wait per idle Claude session via `Stop` + `asyncRewake`; terminal/controller/inbox/stall/unknown-continuation events; private cursor closes fast-finish attach races; no model polling loop. |
+| 1.9 / 2.4 Windows `/tmp` and mutation false-green | Fixed in #15 policy | Workspace/native scratch only; mutation must assert that it actually changed the target before gate interpretation. |
+| 1.10 / 2.10 token economy | Fixed/observable | #14 `sharedContext`, fresh-vs-cached input and cache-hit telemetry; #15 event waits and `noMutationObserved` prevent unnecessary controller/status/model turns. |
+| 1.11 fake “running/queued” progress | Fixed across #14/#15 | Queue blockers name capacity/writer/reservation holder and duration; stalled queues wake Claude; terminal writers with no observed mutation are explicitly flagged. |
+| 1.12 / 3.9 sibling-worktree Python environment | Fixed in #14 | Local `.venv` provenance detects editable distributions outside the admitted worktree before inference; an unproven environment is not reported green. |
+| 2.3 `result --wait` polling/timeouts | Fixed in #15 | Default bounded timeout; one supervisor event wait; timeout returns current lane + blocker as “still running/queued,” not lane failure. |
+| 2.5 gate blind-spot optimization | Guarded in #15 | Standard execution posture forbids passing one gate by moving behavior/data into another gate’s blind spot; verification evidence makes the tradeoff reviewable. |
+| 2.6 source-pinning instead of behavior verification | Guarded in #15 | Templates require behavior checks or explicit rationale when exact source text is itself the contract. Static source-pin detection is intentionally not guessed. |
+| 2.7 report-text anomaly | Fixed/guarded in #15 | Actual Unicode replacement characters are rejected as decode corruption; unusual valid scripts are not heuristically called corrupt. Parent verifies artifact/source before changing code to match prose. |
+| 2.9 cancellation while writes may still be in flight | Fixed in #15 | Interrupt acknowledgement is not terminal acknowledgement. Writer capacity stays reserved until terminal observation; response says `terminalObserved`; touched-file evidence is returned and no rollback is implied. |
+| 2.11 visual/CSS claims without render evidence | Guarded in #15 | Visual/layout claims require browser/image evidence; otherwise verification is `skipped`, `blocked`, or explicitly unverified. |
+| 3.2 verifier cache/temp cleanup blockers | Fixed/guarded in #15 | Read-only verification template uses `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` and pytest `-p no:cacheprovider` where appropriate; controller-only gates are not falsely claimed. |
+| 3.3 / 3.15 old plugin-cache runtime path | Fixed in #15 | Skills use `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` only. Version mismatch blocks mutating Fleet commands until ownership-verified setup/reload; no manual cache-version selection. |
+| 3.4 stale Codex model process | Fixed in #15 | Catalog provenance + idle process refresh + configured-model mismatch guidance. |
+| 3.6 truncated verifier evidence | Fixed across #14/#15 | Longer retained structured evidence plus `result --full`; compact status remains bounded. |
+| 3.7 undiscoverable follow-up syntax | Fixed in #15 | Root and per-command `--help` with exact JSON examples. |
+| 3.8 unavailable real PostgreSQL tests | Guarded, external prerequisite remains external | Verification results distinguish passed/failed/skipped/blocked and name the actual environment. Fleet does not fabricate a PostgreSQL target. |
+| 3.11 contradictory/underspecified parent brief | Guarded in #15 orchestration | Parent Claude performs edge-case/contradiction review before admission; genuine unresolved user choices still stop rather than being guessed by a worker. |
+| 3.13 >1 MiB persisted-thread resume | Fixed in #14 | `excludeTurns:true`, bounded paged recent history, larger bounded broker budget and specific diagnostics. |
+| 3.14 ambiguous continuation permanently holding writer lock | Fixed across #14/#15 | Runtime probing can safely release proven-not-started reservations or rebind started truth; manual release requires evidence; queue status names the lock; CLI exposes `reconcile`. |
+| 3.15 cross-worktree retry lineage | Fixed across #14/#15 | Qualified `<workspaceKey>:<laneId>` lineage is validated against registered source state; unknown/interrupted sources require reconciliation evidence. |
+
+## Deliberate external boundaries
+
+Fleet does **not** pretend to fix project-specific missing infrastructure such as a real PostgreSQL test
+target, a repository-local font asset, or browser access. It also does not guess whether a source-text test
+is semantically wrong or automatically split arbitrary prose into semantic subprojects. Those are judgment or
+project-capability boundaries. The harness now makes each boundary explicit before or in verification, so a
+missing capability is not silently converted into success and does not consume a needless worker turn when a
+zero-inference preflight can prove the blocker.
